{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.62,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "short_to_ground",
      "components": ["J7"],
      "pins": ["J7.1", "J7.2", "J7.3"],
      "nets": ["GND", "BAT+ (VIN/VBUS node)", "NET0048"],
      "observed": "On the EthernetAndPower sheet the DC barrel jack J7 (Barrel_Jack_Switch) carries the note '2 and 3 are shorted with no plug / 1 is center, center is positive'. Tracing the wires, the pin labelled 1 (the center/positive contact) is tied to GND, the pin tied to the BAT+/VIN/VBUS node is 2, and the remaining switch pin is tied to NET0048 (the raw battery-positive node at the anode of U5 / U1+). Thus the center positive pin is shorted to ground and the sleeve/switch contacts do not implement the intended GND / BAT- roles.",
      "expected": "Per the specification the jack must be wired J4.1→BAT+ (center/positive), J4.2→GND (sleeve), J4.3→BAT-, so that the normally-shorted 2-3 pair keeps the battery return connected to GND and a DC plug both powers BAT+ through the center pin and disconnects the battery. The center pin must never be on GND.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "Netlist: J4.1→BAT+ (center/positive), J4.2→GND (sleeve), J4.3→BAT-. Since pins 2 and 3 are normally shorted (per the note)... the jack's internal switch keeps the battery's return path connected to GND by default, and inserting a DC plug breaks that short — disconnecting the battery."},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "a1d9676 \"Meshinger 1.0 rev B WARNING THE DC PLUG PINS ARE WRONG, SHORTS BATTERY!\""},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "EthernetAndPower sheet, J7 'Barrel_Jack_Switch' text note: '2 and 3 are shorted with no plug / 1 is center, center is positive'; pin 1 wire runs to a GND symbol, pin 2 wire runs to the BAT+/VIN/VBUS junction, pin 3 wire runs to NET0048."}
      ],
      "impact": "With a DC adapter plugged in, the adapter's positive center pin is shorted to ground (and the sleeve is held at BAT+), causing a hard short / reversed polarity on the power input; the battery-disconnect logic is also broken. This matches the 'DC plug pins are wrong, shorts battery' failure that the intended rev-D design was supposed to fix.",
      "confidence": 0.62
    }
  ],
  "summary": "All component values and part identities match the specification, but the DC barrel jack J7 on the power sheet is miswired: its center/positive pin is tied to GND and the shorted switch pair does not implement the spec's intended 1→BAT+/2→GND/3→BAT- mapping, shorting the DC input (and mis-handling the battery) — a deviation from the intended design."
}

